{"total":134,"start":1,"num":100,"nextStart":101,"results":[{"id":"1175d62a1b354fafb104638ed0097fa6","owner":"EIA.gov","created":1599321752000,"modified":1739905725000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Natural Gas Storage Regions","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"Natural gas storage regions in the lower 48 States, as of 11/19/2015.<div><br /><\/div><div>U.S. Energy Information Administration, <a href='https://ir.eia.gov/ngs/notice_08_31_2015.html' rel='nofollow ugc' target='_blank'>Weekly Natural Gas Storage Report (Notice)<\/a><br /><\/div>","tags":["Natural Gas","EIA","EIA.gov","Energy","Energy Information Administration","Nonrenewable energy"],"snippet":"Natural gas storage regions in the lower 48 States as defined by the U.S. Energy Information Administration's \"Weekly Natural Gas Storage Report\".  Classification was implemented on 11/19/2015.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1739905724746.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-124.76306799999996,24.523096000000066],[-66.94989499999997,49.38435800000008]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA.gov)","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div>None (public use). Users are advised to thoroughly review the metadata to understand the appropriate use and limitations of the data. These data and related graphics, if available, are not legal documents and are not intended to be used as such.The information contained in these data is dynamic and may change over time. The U.S. Energy Information Administration gives no warranty, expressed or implied, as to the accuracy, reliability, or completeness of these data.<\/div><div><br /><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services7.arcgis.com/FGr1D95XCGALKXqM/arcgis/rest/services/Natural_Gas_Storage_Regions/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1520726,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"FGr1D95XCGALKXqM","scoreCompleteness":95,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"U.S. Energy Information Administration","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"a8c10d8f8d7a4a23a19787925795d6f0","owner":"EIA.gov","created":1687377246000,"modified":1691680396000,"guid":null,"name":"Geographies_wRECSData_DOLELCOL_HH","title":"Geographies_wRECSData_DOLELCOL_HH","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service","View Service"],"description":"<p>We periodically conduct the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>Residential Energy Consumption Survey (RECS)<\/i><\/a>, which provides detailed estimates of energy usage in U.S. homes. This dashboard includes selected residential energy site consumption, expenditures, and household characteristics information from the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>2020 RECS<\/i><\/a>, the 15<sup>th<\/sup> iteration of the survey.<\/p>\n<p>You can find additional information about the <i>2020 RECS<\/i>, including <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/terminology.cfm' rel='nofollow ugc'>terminology<\/a>, <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=methodology' rel='nofollow ugc'>methodology<\/a>,\n<a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=microdata' rel='nofollow ugc'>microdata\nfile<\/a><span>,<\/span> and <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state' rel='nofollow ugc'>data\ntables<\/a>, on our website.<\/p>\n<p>Estimates and relative standard error values are available in the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state#hc' rel='nofollow ugc'>state data tables<\/a>. Perceived differences between the estimates displayed in the bar chart may not be statistically significant.<\/p>\n<p>Notes: Some estimates are not available for all states (<i>Data withheld<\/i>) because either the relative\nstandard error (RSE) was greater than 50% or there were fewer than 10 households in the reporting sample. These are identified as \u201cQ\u201d or \u201cN\u201d in the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state#hc' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>RECS<\/i>\ndata tables<\/a>. Exercise caution when deriving withheld estimates from published estimates.<\/p>\n<p>Data source: U.S. Energy Information Administration, Office of Energy Demand and Integrated Statistics, <i>2020\nResidential Energy Consumption Survey<\/i><\/p>","tags":["Residential Energy Consumption Survey","air conditioning","cooling"],"snippet":"These data include selected residential energy site consumption, expenditures and household characteristics information from the 2020 Residential Energy Consumption Survey (RECS).","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1689792005700.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-179.14892426641455,-14.548692021858761],[179.7784547439671,71.36516173948701]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"U.S. Energy Information Administration","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>None (public use). Users are advised to thoroughly review the metadata to understand the appropriate use and limitations of the data. These data and related graphics, if available, are not legal documents and are not intended to be used as such. The information contained in these data is dynamic and may change over time. The U.S. Energy Information Administration gives no warranty, expressed or implied, as to the accuracy, reliability, or completeness of these data.<\/span>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services7.arcgis.com/FGr1D95XCGALKXqM/arcgis/rest/services/Geographies_wRECSData_DOLELCOL_HH/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":166069,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"FGr1D95XCGALKXqM","scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"U.S. Energy Information Administration","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"506c6f3d0be34c9494fd8057980f679b","owner":"EIA.gov","created":1687372038000,"modified":1691680395000,"guid":null,"name":"Geographies_wRECSData_TOTALBTUSPH_HH","title":"Geographies_wRECSData_TOTALBTUSPH_HH","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service","View Service"],"description":"<p>We periodically conduct the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>Residential Energy Consumption Survey (RECS)<\/i><\/a>, which provides detailed estimates of energy usage in U.S. homes. This dashboard includes selected residential energy site consumption, expenditures, and household characteristics information from the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>2020 RECS<\/i><\/a>, the 15<sup>th<\/sup> iteration of the survey.<\/p>\n<p>You can find additional information about the <i>2020 RECS<\/i>, including <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/terminology.cfm' rel='nofollow ugc'>terminology<\/a>, <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=methodology' rel='nofollow ugc'>methodology<\/a>,\n<a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=microdata' rel='nofollow ugc'>microdata\nfile<\/a><span>,<\/span> and <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state' rel='nofollow ugc'>data\ntables<\/a>, on our website.<\/p>\n<p>Estimates and relative standard error values are available in the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state#hc' rel='nofollow ugc'>state data tables<\/a>. Perceived differences between the estimates displayed in the bar chart may not be statistically significant.<\/p>\n<p>Notes: Some estimates are not available for all states (<i>Data withheld<\/i>) because either the relative\nstandard error (RSE) was greater than 50% or there were fewer than 10 households in the reporting sample. These are identified as \u201cQ\u201d or \u201cN\u201d in the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state#hc' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>RECS<\/i>\ndata tables<\/a>. Exercise caution when deriving withheld estimates from published estimates.<\/p>\n<p>Data source: U.S. Energy Information Administration, Office of Energy Demand and Integrated Statistics, <i>2020\nResidential Energy Consumption Survey<\/i><\/p>","tags":["Residential Energy Consumption Survey","space heating"],"snippet":"These data include selected residential energy site consumption, expenditures and household characteristics information from the 2020 Residential Energy Consumption Survey (RECS).","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1689793679467.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-179.14892426641455,-14.548692021858761],[179.7784547439671,71.36516173948701]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"U.S. Energy Information Administration","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>None (public use). Users are advised to thoroughly review the metadata to understand the appropriate use and limitations of the data. These data and related graphics, if available, are not legal documents and are not intended to be used as such. The information contained in these data is dynamic and may change over time. The U.S. Energy Information Administration gives no warranty, expressed or implied, as to the accuracy, reliability, or completeness of these data.<\/span>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services7.arcgis.com/FGr1D95XCGALKXqM/arcgis/rest/services/Geographies_wRECSData_TOTALBTUSPH_HH/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":165744,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"FGr1D95XCGALKXqM","scoreCompleteness":91,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"U.S. Energy Information Administration","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"bf26111e978d4397ab1bc6109c4290c4","owner":"EIA.gov","created":1687371605000,"modified":1691680393000,"guid":null,"name":"Geographies_wRECSData_GALLONLP_HH","title":"Geographies_wRECSData_GALLONLP_HH","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service","View Service"],"description":"<p>We periodically conduct the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>Residential Energy Consumption Survey (RECS)<\/i><\/a>, which provides detailed estimates of energy usage in U.S. homes. This dashboard includes selected residential energy site consumption, expenditures, and household characteristics information from the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>2020 RECS<\/i><\/a>, the 15<sup>th<\/sup> iteration of the survey.<\/p>\n<p>You can find additional information about the <i>2020 RECS<\/i>, including <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/terminology.cfm' rel='nofollow ugc'>terminology<\/a>, <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=methodology' rel='nofollow ugc'>methodology<\/a>,\n<a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=microdata' rel='nofollow ugc'>microdata\nfile<\/a><span>,<\/span> and <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state' rel='nofollow ugc'>data\ntables<\/a>, on our website.<\/p>\n<p>Estimates and relative standard error values are available in the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state#hc' rel='nofollow ugc'>state data tables<\/a>. Perceived differences between the estimates displayed in the bar chart may not be statistically significant.<\/p>\n<p>Notes: Some estimates are not available for all states (<i>Data withheld<\/i>) because either the relative\nstandard error (RSE) was greater than 50% or there were fewer than 10 households in the reporting sample. These are identified as \u201cQ\u201d or \u201cN\u201d in the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state#hc' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>RECS<\/i>\ndata tables<\/a>. Exercise caution when deriving withheld estimates from published estimates.<\/p>\n<p>Data source: U.S. Energy Information Administration, Office of Energy Demand and Integrated Statistics, <i>2020\nResidential Energy Consumption Survey<\/i><\/p>","tags":["Residential Energy Consumption Survey","propane"],"snippet":"These data include selected residential energy site consumption, expenditures and household characteristics information from the 2020 Residential Energy Consumption Survey (RECS).","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1689793089895.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-179.14892426641455,-14.548692021858761],[179.7784547439671,71.36516173948701]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"U.S. Energy Information Administration","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>None (public use). Users are advised to thoroughly review the metadata to understand the appropriate use and limitations of the data. These data and related graphics, if available, are not legal documents and are not intended to be used as such. The information contained in these data is dynamic and may change over time. The U.S. Energy Information Administration gives no warranty, expressed or implied, as to the accuracy, reliability, or completeness of these data.<\/span>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services7.arcgis.com/FGr1D95XCGALKXqM/arcgis/rest/services/Geographies_wRECSData_GALLONLP_HH/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":164610,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"FGr1D95XCGALKXqM","scoreCompleteness":91,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"U.S. Energy Information Administration","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"e69e60839d214b4fbc36db55347f0ee6","owner":"EIA.gov","created":1685712254000,"modified":1691680152000,"guid":null,"name":"Geographies_wRECSData","title":"Geographies_wRECSData","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><p><\/p><p style='margin-left:.5in;'>We periodically conduct the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>Residential Energy\nConsumption Survey (RECS)<\/i><\/a>, which provides detailed estimates of energy\nusage in U.S. homes. This dashboard includes selected residential energy site\nconsumption, expenditures, and household characteristics information from the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>2020 RECS<\/i><\/a>,\nthe 15<sup>th<\/sup> iteration of the survey.<\/p>\n\n<p style='margin-left:.5in;'>You can find additional information\nabout 2020 RECS, including <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/terminology.cfm' rel='nofollow ugc'>terminology<\/a>,\n<a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=methodology' rel='nofollow ugc'>methodology<\/a>,\n<a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=microdata' rel='nofollow ugc'>microdata\nfile<\/a> and <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state' rel='nofollow ugc'>data\ntables<\/a>, on our website.<\/p>\n\n<p style='margin-left:.5in;'>Notes: Some estimates are not available for all states (<i>Data withheld<\/i>) because either the relative standard error (RSE) was greater than 50% or there were fewer than 10 households in the reporting sample. These are identified as \u201cQ\u201d or \u201cN\u201d in the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state#hc' rel='nofollow ugc'><i>RECS<\/i> data tables<\/a>. Exercise caution when deriving withheld estimates from published estimates.<br /><\/p>\n\n<p style='margin-left:.5in;'>Estimates and relative standard\nerror values are available in the <a href='https://www.eia.gov/consumption/residential/data/2020/index.php?view=state#hc' rel='nofollow ugc'>state\ndata tables<\/a>. Perceived differences between the estimates displayed in the\nbar chart may not be statistically significant.<\/p>\n\n<p style='margin-left:.5in;'>Data source: U.S. Energy\nInformation Administration, Office of Energy Demand and Integrated Statistics, <i>2020\nResidential Energy Consumption Survey<\/i> <\/p><br /><p><\/p><\/div>","tags":["Residential Energy Consumption Survey","household energy","square footage","site consumption","space heating","air conditioning","refrigerators","water heating","all-electric","natural gas","electricity","propane","fuel oil"],"snippet":"These data include selected residential energy site consumption, expenditures and household characteristics information from the 2020 Residential Energy Consumption Survey (RECS).","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-179.14892426641455,-14.548692021858761],[179.7784547439671,71.36516173948701]],"categories":["/Categories/Electricity","/Categories/Natural Gas"],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"U.S. Energy Information Administration","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>None (public use). Users are advised to thoroughly review the metadata to understand the appropriate use and limitations of the data. These data and related graphics, if available, are not legal documents and are not intended to be used as such. The information contained in these data is dynamic and may change over time. The U.S. Energy Information Administration gives no warranty, expressed or implied, as to the accuracy, reliability, or completeness of these data.<\/span>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services7.arcgis.com/FGr1D95XCGALKXqM/arcgis/rest/services/Geographies_wRECSData/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":168798,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"FGr1D95XCGALKXqM","scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"U.S. Energy Information Administration","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"3f001fba00dc4add8dbd00542d61e4da","owner":"EIA.gov","created":1591722535000,"modified":1739904635000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Tight Oil and Shale Gas Plays","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><p><span>General areas for shale plays in the U.S. This 2021 update includes additions of formation benches for <\/span>Spraberry and Wolfcamp in Midland Basin. <\/p><p><span>Source: EIA based on Enverus DrillingInfo Inc., the U.S. Geological Survey, publicly available peer-reviewed research papers, academic theses, and publications of State Geological Agencies. <br /><\/span><\/p><\/div>","tags":["resources","tight oil","shale","EIA","EIA.gov","Energy","U.S. Energy Information Administration"],"snippet":"This data was created for the purpose of identifying and providing information on shale plays in the United States. ","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1739904634779.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-121.14788999999998,27.489075000000064],[-74.82692527599994,48.99999999937189]],"categories":["/Categories/Oil and Gas Plays"],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"U.S. Energy Information Administration, Enverus DrillingInfo Inc., the U.S. Geological Survey","classification":null,"lic