in the Appalachian Basin. Utica is a stacked play consisting of the Utica formation and underlying Point Pleasant formation. Source: U.S. Energy Information Administration based on data from various published studies as of May 2016.\n","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1739905413568.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-82.66439371199992,38.917874907000055],[-74.82692527599994,42.902870724000046]],"categories":["/Categories/Oil and Gas Plays"],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"U.S. Energy Information Administration","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN><SPAN>The U.S. Energy Information Administration shall not be held liable for improper or incorrect use of the data described and/or contained herein. These data and related graphics, if available, are not legal documents and are not intended to be used as such. The information contained in these data is dynamic and may change over time. The U.S. Energy Information Administration gives no warranty, expressed or implied, as to the accuracy, reliability, or completeness of these data.<\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN /><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services7.arcgis.com/FGr1D95XCGALKXqM/arcgis/rest/services/ShalePlay_Utica_Boundary_EIA_May2016/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":33442,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"FGr1D95XCGALKXqM","scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"U.S. Energy Information Administration","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"de4fa6aae20147d9a3d59fb165f780ab","owner":"EIA.gov","created":1776193788000,"modified":1776971974000,"guid":null,"name":"Petroleum_Administration_for_Defense_Districts__PADD____Subdistricts","title":"Petroleum Administration for Defense Districts  (PADD) - Subdistricts","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><div><p><span>This dataset provides a standardized spatial representation of the Petroleum Administration for Defense Districts (PADDs) across the 50 U.S. states and the District of Columbia. It includes PADDs 2\u20135 in their standard form and subdivides PADD 1 into its three subdistricts\u2014PADD 1A, 1B, and 1C\u2014to support more detailed analysis of the East Coast region.  These districts support consistent regional analysis of petroleum supply, refining activity, transportation patterns, and market conditions. The dataset enables integration with federal and state energy statistics and supports mapping, visualization, and analytical workflows that require regionally aggregated petroleum data.<\/span><\/p><p><span>PADD 6 and PADD 7, which apply to U.S. territories, are not included.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["EIA","U.S. Energy Information Administration","regions","petroleum","oil/petroleum","PADD","PADD 1"],"snippet":"A geographic aggregation of the 50 U.S. states and the District of Columbia into Petroleum Administration for Defense Districts, with PADD 1 (East Coast) represented as three subdistricts (1A, 1B, 1C).","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-179.14703899994987,18.914186999630378],[179.77434399997568,71.38057799957505]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p><span style='background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(74,74,74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='display:inline 